# GraveYield console — environment configuration example.
# Copy to .env.local (dev) or set in your deployment platform.

# ── Snapshot artifact source (P4.1 Step 1 legacy / P4.1 Step 2 stable pointer) ──
# The Graveyard reads the grave-indexer ConsoleSnapshot artifact through
# /api/gy/snapshot. Three topologies exist; configure EXACTLY ONE (mixing
# them is rejected as SOURCE_CONFLICT — the console refuses to guess).
#
# PRODUCTION (stable-pointer resolver, P4.1 Step 2):
#   GY_SNAPSHOT_GITHUB_REPO — "owner/repo" holding the dedicated stable
#     reference refs/tags/console-snapshot-prod and the workflow-protected
#     --latest=false versioned releases ("workflow-protected" = the
#     publisher workflow's --latest=false convention plus pointer digest
#     verification; this is NOT GitHub's owner-enabled immutable-releases
#     platform feature, whose enablement is a separate setting that must
#     be verified independently). The resolver walks the approved
#     production chain: stable ref → annotated tag object (stable-pointer
#     JSON) → versioned release assets, verifying every asset's SHA-256 and
#     byte length against the pointer before the fail-closed schema-v2
#     parser runs. Works unauthenticated while the repository is public
#     (standard GitHub API rate limit applies).
#   GY_SNAPSHOT_STABLE_REF  — optional; default "console-snapshot-prod".
#   GY_SNAPSHOT_GITHUB_TOKEN — OPTIONAL server-side GitHub token for
#     authenticated reads (rate-limit headroom on shared egress IPs).
#     Server-side only: never embedded in client code, never logged.
#
# LEGACY (direct artifact URL / mounted volume — still supported for local
# development and self-hosted runs; NOT the production path under the
# dedicated-reference architecture, and unable to enforce pointer digests):
#   GY_SNAPSHOT_URL  — HTTPS artifact store (any GET endpoint).
#   GY_SNAPSHOT_PATH — absolute path to console-snapshot.json on a mounted
#                      indexer output volume.
#
# Setting both a legacy source and GY_SNAPSHOT_GITHUB_REPO is rejected
# (SOURCE_CONFLICT) — the console refuses to guess.
#GY_SNAPSHOT_GITHUB_REPO="GraveYield/grave-indexer"
#GY_SNAPSHOT_STABLE_REF="console-snapshot-prod"
#GY_SNAPSHOT_URL="https://artifacts.example/gy/console-snapshot.json"
#GY_SNAPSHOT_PATH="/var/lib/grave-indexer/console-snapshot.json"

# ── Fleet state source (P4.3 fleet ingestion) ─────────────────────────
# The Salvor Fleet view reads the salvor fleet's JSONL trails
# (monitor-events.jsonl + alerts.jsonl) through /api/gy/fleet. Point this
# at the fleet-ops FLEET_STATE_DIR the operator mounts (self-hosted /
# Docker). Unset → the view honestly renders "unavailable"; it never
# falls back to simulated bots.
#
#   GY_FLEET_STATE_PATH — absolute path to the mounted FLEET_STATE_DIR
#                         (the directory holding the fleet's JSONL trails).
#
# There is deliberately no URL topology here: no upstream publisher of
# fleet trails exists today (see docs/fleet-ingestion.md).
#GY_FLEET_STATE_PATH="/var/lib/salvor-bots/fleet-state"

# Optional freshness budget for the fleet trail in ms (default 1800000 =
# 30 min — 30× the monitor sweep and 6× the scout cycle cadence). Must be
# a positive integer; anything else is rejected, not guessed.
#GY_FLEET_MAX_AGE_MS="1800000"

# ── Wallet connection ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RPC endpoint for the devnet protocol pulse + wallet balance reads.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL="https://api.devnet.solana.com"

# ── Claims distribution source (P4.4 LP claims integration) ──────────
# The LP Claims view reads the grave-snapshotter's SEALED SnapshotArtifact
# (Merkle root + per-holder leaves/proofs + reconciliation identity) through
# /api/gy/claims. Configure EXACTLY ONE source; with neither set, the view
# honestly renders "snapshot unavailable" — eligibility is unknown, never
# guessed.
#
#   GY_CLAIMS_URL   — HTTPS artifact store (serverless deploys): publish the
#                     sealed distribution JSON to a release asset / object
#                     storage / any GET endpoint.
#   GY_CLAIMS_PATH  — absolute path to the sealed artifact on a mounted
#                     snapshotter output volume (self-hosted / Docker).
#
# The artifact is integrity-verified on every request (whole tree re-derived
# through the vendored canonical SDK) and bound to the on-chain PoolRegistry
# root before any proof is honored. Other holders' rows never leave the
# server — only the queried wallet's own row is served.
#GY_CLAIMS_URL="https://artifacts.example/gy/distribution.json"
#GY_CLAIMS_PATH="/var/lib/grave-snapshotter/distribution.json"

# Optional: freshness budget for the sealed distribution in ms
# (default 604800000 = 7 days — a historical record; the on-chain root is
# the real anchor). Must be a positive integer; anything else is rejected.
#GY_CLAIMS_MAX_AGE_MS="604800000"

# Optional: RPC host for the claims-side on-chain reads
# (default api.devnet.solana.com — devnet only).
#GY_CLAIMS_RPC_HOST="api.devnet.solana.com"
